# prompt: small bird chirping three times
# tags: bird, chirp, animal, nature
# Three sweeps in 300 ms, and the middle one goes down while the others go up.
# A bird call that sweeps the same way every time reads as a machine — the
# alternation is what an ear built to notice birds is actually listening for.
sound "bird chirp" 400ms
  air: noise white >> bp ~5000Hz[2500..9000] Q6 | gain 0.06 decay 300ms
  one: chirp sine ~2600Hz[1400..5000] -> 4200Hz in 60ms | gain 0.3 attack 5ms decay 80ms
  two: chirp sine ~3000Hz[1600..5500] -> 2000Hz in 70ms | gain 0.24 attack 5ms decay 90ms delay 130ms
  three: chirp sine ~3400Hz[1800..6000] -> 4600Hz in 50ms | gain 0.2 attack 5ms decay 80ms delay 260ms
